# --- Push credentials -------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment secrets, never committed. See docs/PUSH_SETUP.md for where each
# one comes from and where it belongs.
frontend/android/app/google-services.json
frontend/ios/BeepMyDevice/GoogleService-Info.plist
backend/*.p8
backend/AuthKey_*.p8
# APPLE_KEY_PATH points here by default. Ignored as a whole directory, not by
# extension: the Firebase service-account download is a .json, and .json is not
# otherwise ignored anywhere.
secrets/

# Gradle build cache. Regenerated on every build; never committed.
frontend/android/.gradle/
frontend/ios/build/

# The Android SDK location, written by Android Studio or by hand before a
# gradlew run. It is one absolute path from one machine ("C:\Users\...\Sdk"),
# so committing it breaks the build for everybody else.
#
# The `android/local.properties` rule further up does NOT cover this: a pattern
# with a slash in the middle is anchored to the directory holding .gitignore,
# so it only ever matched a top-level android/ that this repo does not have.
# Same for its `android/build/` and `android/app/build/` neighbours -- those
# happen to be covered by the bare `build/` rule instead, which matches at any
# depth.
frontend/android/local.properties

# Build and run logs from scripts/androidrun.sh / scripts/applerun.sh. They are
# written beside the scripts that produce them. One file per invocation, named
# by timestamp, so the directory only grows.
frontend/scripts/logs/

# Build outputs. `build/` above catches the Gradle and Xcode output trees
# wherever they appear; these are the artefacts that land outside one.
frontend/android/app/release/
*.apk
*.aab
*.aar

# Web builds
web/dist/
frontend/web/dist/

# --- Design exports ---------------------------------------------------------
# Raw drops from claude.ai/design, downloaded with the browser's own numbering
# ("Design decision chat (2)"). They are an inbox, not a source: the canvas the
# code is built against is the copy under frontend/docs/design/, which carries
# stable filenames so a new export overwrites the old one and git holds the
# previous version. Ignoring the drop is what stops a numbered duplicate
# sitting beside the current design, which has pointed the docs at a stale
# canvas before.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: bare `design/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently swallows frontend/docs/design/ -- the
# checked-in canvas the coding-style skill names as the authority.
/design/
